      "role": "cite",
      "name": "requirements.cli.mdbook",
      "commentary": ""
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`Definition` (src/lib.rs lines 121–126) is a plain data record with `path`, `text` and `kind` fields. It is not a test, and it implements no part of `requirements.cli.mdbook`: it makes no decision, check or output, and the requirement says nothing about the shape of a definition record. The behavior the requirement states, rendering definitions and linked badges as the mdBook preprocessor, lives in `preprocess_book` (src/lib.rs lines 176–272), which carries the `{impl}`.\n\n`preprocess_book` builds `Definition` values from the book chapters. `reference_badge` and `replace_inline_references` in the same file, and `src/index.rs` for the detail pages, use them to link badges and render definitions. A change to the rendering requirement could therefore require changing this struct, so `{cite}` is the right role. The struct has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same requirement, so the citation is not redundant. I found no gap.",
  "inputs": [
